The root cause is now concrete: this audit container’s process namespace reports small PIDs (for example `2`), while its mounted `/proc` exposes different host PIDs, so Lean’s `/proc/<getpid>/exe` lookup fails even though `/proc/self/exe` works. I’ll apply a narrow audit-local `readlink` compatibility shim that rewrites only `/proc/<digits>/exe` to `/proc/self/exe`; it does not alter Lean inputs, source, elaboration, or proof checking. I’ll record the shim source/hash and use it for both the repeated preflight and fresh clean build.
